# The U2B hardware manual is 173 MB -- it is 10,221 pages and ships every
# peripheral chapter. Committing it would put a permanent, unshrinkable
# blob in the history for a file that is one download away, so it stays on
# disk and out of git. The other PDFs here are in line with docs/arm and
# docs/st and are tracked.
#
#   https://www.renesas.com/en/document/mah/rh850u2b-hardware-users-manual-rev-130-r01uh0923ej0130
#
# The name below is the file as it actually lands from that link. It was
# previously written as "...-rh850u2b-hardware-manual.pdf", which matches
# nothing -- a .gitignore entry that silently does not apply, so the blob
# was staged anyway the first time anything ran `git add -A`.
r01uh0923ej0130-rh850u2b.pdf

# The toolchain installer, its licence manager and the Y-ASK board package
# are 175 MB between them, and the same argument applies: all three are
# vendor downloads rather than anything this repo produces, and the
# installers are licensed software that should not be redistributed here.
# The Dockerfile beside this file is what turns the first two into the
# ccrh:latest image the G4MH guest is built with.
cc-rh_v20800/
license-manager_v20900/
Y-ASK-RH850U2B-v0200/
